Release 1.1 Dev Changes

 - use Orthanc study UUID for filename- none of this mrn/session stuff

 - pick up more data from the Dicom object and use some of it to pre-fill
   in some items (like age of patient). Further items may be presented
   in a new header at the top as read-only information for the radiologist

 - add a code dark study tool which is a way to see the list of studies still either
   needing to begin or continue reviewing, see studies that need to be signed, and
   see studies that need to be printed. You can also delete reports begun but not
   yet signed.

 - get icons back on the desktop for both code dark configurator and code dark study tool

 - change all the packaging around and build more. We no longer depend upon any orthanc
   packages from ubuntu itself- we only depend upon things like libboost and dcmtk. This
   also allows us to build newer pieces since we're getting them direct from Orthanc
   mercurial

- Have a build cache for things we need to download

- Solve some of the build problems we've begun to have with OHIF- this requires running
  passwordless sudo for part of that built (for cleaning note that git clean -xdf won't
  clean, silently, files that have root permissions in root owned subdirectories).

- Continue to update the documentation as we go along. We've managed to move on to Ubuntu 24.04.3.
